ned the ed25519 host key into /etc/ssh/ssh_host_ed25519_key-cert.pub (principals node1, 10.100.239.10), configured sshd with HostCertificate, fixed an SELinux mislabel (tmp_t -> sshd_key_t) that was blocking sshd from loading the cert, and verified a client trusting only the CA (@cert-authority entry, no pinned host key, StrictHostKeyChecking=yes) connects successfully both before and after a full node restart. Node1 was restarted once via the native reboot mechanism; boot_id changed from 5fb1b173... to d57d6d0a..., and the CA/certificate configuration and successful cert-based SSH connection were re-verified afterward.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Captured baseline: sshd active, ed25519 host key present, boot_id 5fb1b173-c1c8-4647-b118-0145511f0fcc\",\"Generated ED25519 SSH CA keypair at /etc/ssh/ca/ssh_ca_key on node1\",\"Signed the node1 ed25519 host public key with the CA as a host certificate with principals node1 and 10.100.239.10, valid 52 weeks\",\"Added HostCertificate directive to sshd_config, validated with sshd -t, reloaded/restarted sshd\",\"Diagnosed and fixed SELinux context (tmp_t -> sshd_key_t) that was silently preventing sshd from loading the host certificate\",\"Built a client-side known_hosts containing only an @cert-authority CA trust anchor (no host key pinning) and a throwaway client keypair authorized on node1\",\"Verified with StrictHostKeyChecking=yes that the client accepted the server purely via the CA-signed certificate ('matches the ED25519-CERT host certificate') and executed a command\",\"Captured pre-restart boot_id and health, triggered a background-delayed 'sudo reboot' so the ack returned before disconnect\",\"Polled node1 until exec was available again and confirmed boot_id changed (d57d6d0a-3bb6-470f-9c6d-4039b98c4e55)\",\"Re-verified sshd active, HostCertificate loaded with correct SELinux label, and re-ran the CA-trust-only SSH connection test successfully post-restart\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"SSH CA created on node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-2d51ffc292834d81\"],\"summary\":\"ssh-keygen generated CA keypair at /etc/ssh/ca/ssh_ca_key with fingerprint SHA256:IXSC9lpHS...H/Q\"},{\"requirement\":\"Host certificate signed by the CA and served by sshd\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-b290cedbf7344888\",\"cmd-351c1d22b27945b9\"],\"summary\":\"ssh-keygen -s signed the ed25519 host key with principals node1,10.100.239.10; sshd -T confirms hostcertificate directive active\"},{\"requirement\":\"Client trusting only the CA (no host-key pinning) connects successfully\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-ea117e76f1954aa9\"],\"summary\":\"Verbose SSH log shows 'Host is known and matches the ED25519-CERT host certificate', 'Found CA key in /tmp/ca_known_hosts', successful auth and command execution CONNECTED_VIA_CA_CERT/node1, using only an @cert-authority known_hosts entry with StrictHostKeyChecking=yes\"},{\"requirement\":\"Root cause fix: SELinux blocked cert loading (diagnostic honesty)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-a35c590efdb64a98\",\"cmd-aa5331de7c944360\",\"cmd-6bb4eb903a1e4493\",\"cmd-212448f718d1415a\"],\"summary\":\"journalctl showed 'Could not load host certificate'; ls -Z revealed tmp_t context; chcon to sshd_key_t and sshd restart resolved it, confirmed by absence of new errors\"},{\"requirement\":\"Pre-restart healthy baseline and boot identity\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-0b63503bd31341bb\",\"cmd-7cb55c8272d4418a\"],\"summary\":\"boot_id 5fb1b173-c1c8-4647-b118-0145511f0fcc captured before restart alongside sshd active and hostcertificate config confirmed\"},{\"requirement\":\"Restart acknowledgement returned before disconnect\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-db76cdd6e53f41ce\"],\"summary\":\"Backgrounded 'sleep 2; sudo reboot' returned pid=1696 immediately, ack received before node went down\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node restart proof via changed boot identity\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-df7ed3c8f83d4cf2\",\"cmd-79e6fcd16093489f\",\"cmd-387fafa5469f4efb\"],\"summary\":\"Poll sequence: same boot_id, then connection timed