chor (no host key pinning) and a throwaway client keypair authorized on node1","Verified with StrictHostKeyChecking=yes that the client accepted the server purely via the CA-signed certificate ('matches the ED25519-CERT host certificate') and executed a command","Captured pre-restart boot_id and health, triggered a background-delayed 'sudo reboot' so the ack returned before disconnect","Polled node1 until exec was available again and confirmed boot_id changed (d57d6d0a-3bb6-470f-9c6d-4039b98c4e55)","Re-verified sshd active, HostCertificate loaded with correct SELinux label, and re-ran the CA-trust-only SSH connection test successfully post-restart"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"SSH CA created on node1","command_ids":["cmd-2d51ffc292834d81"],"summary":"ssh-keygen generated CA keypair at /etc/ssh/ca/ssh_ca_key with fingerprint SHA256:IXSC9lpHS...H/Q"},{"requirement":"Host certificate signed by the CA and served by sshd","command_ids":["cmd-b290cedbf7344888","cmd-351c1d22b27945b9"],"summary":"ssh-keygen -s signed the ed25519 host key with principals node1,10.100.239.10; sshd -T confirms hostcertificate directive active"},{"requirement":"Client trusting only the CA (no host-key pinning) connects successfully","command_ids":["cmd-ea117e76f1954aa9"],"summary":"Verbose SSH log shows 'Host is known and matches the ED25519-CERT host certificate', 'Found CA key in /tmp/ca_known_hosts', successful auth and command execution CONNECTED_VIA_CA_CERT/node1, using only an @cert-authority known_hosts entry with StrictHostKeyChecking=yes"},{"requirement":"Root cause fix: SELinux blocked cert loading (diagnostic honesty)","command_ids":["cmd-a35c590efdb64a98","cmd-aa5331de7c944360","cmd-6bb4eb903a1e4493","cmd-212448f718d1415a"],"summary":"journalctl showed 'Could not load host certificate'; ls -Z revealed tmp_t context; chcon to sshd_key_t and sshd restart resolved it, confirmed by absence of new errors"},{"requirement":"Pre-restart healthy baseline and boot identity","command_ids":["cm